Xsynth 2000 - version 0.1.1
Vendor: Phaos

Xsynth 2000 is a new digital synthesizer developed from Steve J. Brookes'
Xsynth 1.0.2 (1999).
The faithful/reference edition remains the separate product Xsynth.

Xsynth 2000 provides independently selectable CLASSIC/CLEAN oscillators,
FM/PM and sync, digital mixer/filter modes, polyphony, expanded envelopes,
twelve modulation routes, four independent LFOs, Unison, and six visual themes.
STEEL is the default. The title reads XSYNTH 2000, followed by small v0.1.1 text.

Build: ./build.ps1 (Windows, CMake, Visual Studio, official VST3 SDK).
Pre-build DSP gate: ./validate-dsp.ps1 (test executables only).
See DSP_VALIDATION.md for results, the envelope precision fix, and retained WAVs.
The full build runs this gate before compiling a VST3.
Bundle: build/VST3/Release/Xsynth 2000.vst3
Release downloads: Xsynth-2000-0.1.1-Windows-x64.zip and matching source ZIP.
package.ps1 is retained as a historical checkpoint script, not the release workflow.
See PRODUCT-IDENTITY.md, THEMES.md, and CREDITS.md for details.

Existing Xsynth 2000 class IDs, parameter/state formats and theme preferences
remain compatible. The original Xsynth sources and binary are preserved in the
parent workspace and build independently.

Both oscillator Pitch controls now span 0.25..4.0, with old native state migration.
See PITCH_RANGE.md for mapping, automation implications and 239/239 DSSI imports.

Historical bank import (source/test checkpoint): LOAD PATCH -> Import Xsynth-DSSI
Bank... supports format 0 and 1. Conversion has documented limitations; genuine
DSSI listening comparison remains outstanding. See DSSI_COMPATIBILITY.md.
No release VST3 was produced for this importer checkpoint.

Historical README from the original Xsynth 1.0.2 source follows unchanged.
